# CS 6250 Fall 2025 - SDN Firewall Project with POX
# build gibson-29
#
# This file contains the rules for the firewall as specified in the Project Documentation.  
#
# Rule Format:
# RuleNumber,Action,Source MAC,Destination MAC,Source IP,Destination IP,Protocol,Source Port,Destination Port,Comment/Note
# RuleNumber = this is a rule number to help you track a particular rule - it is not used in the firewall implementation
# Action = Block or Allow , Allow Rules need to take precedence over Block Rules
# Source / Destination MAC address in form of xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx
# Source / Destination IP Address in form of xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx/xx in CIDR notation
# Protocol = integer IP protocol number per IANA (0-254)
# Source / Destination Port = if Protocol is TCP or UDP, this is the Application Port Number per IANA
# Comment/Note = this is for your use in tracking rules.
#
# Any field not being used for a match should have a '-' character as it's entry (except for RuleNumber/Comment)
# Do not pad any of the entries (i.e., have a rule like:  1, Block, -, -,...)
#
# Warning:  For the IP address, you need to specify an appropriate network address
# that matches the subnet mask you are using.  For instance, if you want to use a /16
# subnet mask, then the IP address must be x.x.0.0.  For example, a proper address to 
# reference a 192.168.10.x/24 network would be 192.168.10.0/24.  A single host
# is addressed as a single IP address with a /32.  In other words, the host bit for a 
# subnet other than /32 must be 0.
#
# Example Rules:
101,Block,-,-,10.0.0.1/32,10.0.1.0/24,6,-,80,Block 10.0.0.1 from accessing a web server on the 10.0.1.0/24 network
201,Allow,-,-,10.0.0.1/32,10.0.1.125/32,6,-,80,Allow 10.0.0.1 to access a web server on 10.0.1.125 overriding previous rule
1,Block,-,-,10.0.30.4/32,-,6,-,-,Task 1: Block 10.0.30.4 (cn4) from initiating TCP calls
2.1,Block,-,-,10.0.30.5/32,-,-,-,-,Task 2.1: Block 10.0.30.5 (cn5) from initiating any calls
2.2,Block,-,-,-,10.0.30.5/32,-,-,-,Task 2.2: Block 10.0.30.5 (cn5) from receiving any calls
3.1,Block,-,-,-,10.0.1.0/24,1,-,-,Task 3.1: Block us subnet from receiving ICMP pings
3.2,Block,-,-,-,10.0.20.0/24,1,-,-,Task 3.2: Block in subnet from receiving ICMP pings
3.3,Block,-,-,-,10.0.40.0/24,1,-,-,Task 3.3: Block uk subnet from receiving ICMP pings
3.4,Allow,-,-,10.0.0.0/24,-,1,-,-,Task 3.4: Allow HQ to send any ICMP pings (overrides rules 3.1 - 3.4)
4.1,Block,-,-,10.0.30.3/32,-,6,80,-,Task 4.1: Block 10.0.30.3 (cn3) from sending any TCP HTTP calls
4.2,Block,-,-,10.0.30.3/32,-,6,443,-,Task 4.2: Block 10.0.30.3 (cn3) from sending any TCP HTTPS calls
5.1,Block,-,-,10.0.40.128/30,10.0.1.32/31,6,-,9520,Task 5.1: Block uk2-uk5 from accessing service on us3-us4 on TCP Port 9520
5.2,Block,-,-,10.0.20.125/31,10.0.1.32/31,6,-,9520,Task 5.2: Block in4-5 from accessing service on us3-us4 on TCP Port 9520
5.3,Block,-,-,10.0.1.125/32,10.0.1.32/31,6,-,9520,Task 5.3: Block us5 from accessing service on us3-us4 on TCP Port 9520
5.4,Block,-,-,10.0.0.220/32,10.0.1.32/31,6,-,9520,Task 5.4: Block hq5 from accessing service on us3-us4 on TCP Port 9520
6,Block,00:00:00:01:00:1e,-,-,-,17,-,-,Task 6: Block us1 MAC address from making any UDP requests
7.1,Block,-,-,-,10.0.0.0/24,6,-,25,Task 7.1: Block requests to hq subnet's TCP Port 25
7.2,Block,-,-,-,10.0.1.0/24,6,-,25,Task 7.2: Block requests to us subnet's TCP Port 25
7.3,Block,-,-,-,10.0.20.0/24,6,-,25,Task 7.3: Block requests to in subnet's TCP Port 25
7.4,Block,-,-,-,10.0.30.0/24,6,-,25,Task 7.4: Block requests to cn subnet's TCP Port 25
7.5,Block,-,-,-,10.0.40.0/24,6,-,25,Task 7.5: Block requests to uk subnet's TCP Port 25
